This package ports project-owned code from bin9208/openpilot-rust at the
issue-219 development base dev1d811b2f, retaining the repository MIT license.

Source units: openpilot/selfdrive/carrot/carrot_man.py, carrot_serv.py,
curve_speed.py, carrot_navi_control.py, navigation_ingress.py,
navigation_sources.py, navigation_runtime.py, naver_navigation_protocol.py,
server/services/web_settings.py (required upload settings only), and
openpilot/selfdrive/apilot.py (the reachable small Params backup).

The independently registered Carrot Navi receiver is a separate owner and
protocol. This package does not replace it. The existing Rust navd Coordinate,
route limiter, Params, cereal/msgq, Python JSON/numeric support and upload
transport are reused at their existing boundaries.

Retained native external dependencies: GEOS C ABI and implementation when
configured (optional original Shapely behavior; pinned artifacts and licenses
in native-dependencies.json, LICENSE_GEOS and SHAPELY-LICENSE), ZeroMQ and msgq
transport dependencies declared by their crates, shell/tmux for diagnostics,
and sudo/date/system zoneinfo for the original non-PC time-setting boundary.
No project-owned Python runtime is executed by this package.

The original encoded notification URL is retained without adding decoded
credentials. Runtime resolution and disable/override precedence follow the
source. Validation must use owned loopback endpoints and fixture command
boundaries; normal startup/upload and device acceptance remain separate gates.
